-F","gloss_en":"lordship","definition_en":"κυριότης, -ητος, ἡ\n (κύριος), \nlordship, dominion: Eph.1:21, 2Pe.2:10, Ju 8; pl., Col.1:16 (cf. Lft., Col; Mayor, Ju., in ll.; DB, i, 616 f.).†\n (AS)","source_line":3159}],"occurrence_count":4,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"domínio","count":1},{"gloss":"governos","count":1},{"gloss":"o-senhorio","count":1},{"gloss":"soberania","count":1}]},"G3164":{"id":"G3164","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G3164","disambiguated_id":"G3164 =","unique_id":"G3164","headword":"μάχομαι","transliteration":"machomai","lexical_morphology":"G:V","gloss_en":"to quarrel","definition_en":"μάχομαι \n [in LXX chiefly for רִיב, also for נָצָה ni., etc. ;] \n__1. to fight: Act.7:26. \n __2. to quarrel, dispute: 2Ti.2:24, Jas.4:2; πρὸς ἀλλήλους, Jhn.6:52 (cf. δια-μάχομαι).†\n (AS)","source_line":3376}],"occurrence_count":4,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"discutiam","count":1},{"gloss":"que-brigavam","count":1},{"gloss":"brigar","count":1},{"gloss":"combateis","count":1}]},"G3173":{"id":"G3173","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G3173","disambiguated_id":"G3173 =","unique_id":"G3173","headword":"μέγας","transliteration":"megas","lexical_morphology":"G:A","gloss_en":"great","definition_en":"μέγας, μεγάλη, μέγα, \n [in LXX chiefly for גָּדוֹל, also for מַרְבֶּה ,רַב (incl. μείζων), רֹב (μέγιστος) ;] \ngreat; \n__1. of external form, bodily size, measure, extent: λίθος, Mat.2:60; δράκων, Rev.12:3; ἰχθῦς, Jhn.21:11; πόλις, Rev.11:8; μάχαιρα, Rev.6:4, al. \n __2. Of intensity and degree: δύναμις, Act.4:33; φόβος, Mrk.4:41; ἀγάπη, Jhn.15:13; ἄνεμος, 'ib. 6:18; κραυγή, Act.23:9; φῶς, Mat.4:16; πυρετός, Luk.4:38; θλίψις, Mat.24:21. \n __3. Of rank; \n__(a) of persons: θεός (MM, xvi), Tit.2:13; Ἄρτεμις, Act.19:27; compar. (see infr.), Mat.18:1 (cf. Dalman, Words, 113f.); neut. for masc. (Bl., §32, 1), Mat.12:6; \n __(b) of things: ἁμαρτία, Jhn.19:11; μυστήριον, Eph.5:32; = μεγίστη (see infr., and cf. Field, Notes, 16f.), Mat.22:36; compar. for superl. (M, Pr., 78), 1Co.13:13. \n __4. \n__(a) Compar., μείζων: Mat.11:11 23:17, al.; neut. pl., μείζονα, contr. μείζω, Jhn.1:51; double compar., μειζότερος (M, Pr., 236; Bl., §11, 4), III Jo 4; \n __(b) superl, μέγιστος (Deiss., BS, 365), 2Pe.1:4.\n (AS)","source_line":3385}],"occurrence_count":240,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"grande","count":142},{"gloss":"maior","count":40},{"gloss":"grandes","count":23},{"gloss":"alta","count":21},{"gloss":"maiores","count":5},{"gloss":"muito","count":3},{"gloss":"mais","count":1},{"gloss":"grandemente","count":1},{"gloss":"mais-velho","count":1},{"gloss":"muita","count":1},{"gloss":"mais-rigoroso","count":1},{"gloss":"forte","count":1}]},"G3645":{"id":"G3645","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G3645","disambiguated_id":"G3645 =","unique_id":"G3645","headword":"ὀλοθρεύω","transliteration":"olothreuō","lexical_morphology":"G:V","gloss_en":"to destroy","definition_en":"ὀλοθρεύω\n (ὄλεθρος), late (Alex.) form of ὄλεθρεύω ω (cf. MGr., ξολοθρεύω) [in LXX for כָּרַת, שָׁחַת hi., etc. ;] \nto destroy: Heb.11:28 (cf. ἐξ-ολοθρεύω).†\n ὀλεθρεύω, see: ὀλοθρεύω \n ὀλοθρεύω\n (ὄλεθρος), late (Alex.) form of ὄλεθρεύω ω (cf. MGr., ξολοθρεύω) [in LXX for כָּרַת, שָׁחַת hi., etc. ;] \nto destroy: Heb.11:28 (cf. ἐξ-ολοθρεύω).†\n ὀλεθρεύω, see: ὀλοθρεύω \n (AS)","source_line":3761}],"occurrence_count":1,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"destruidor","count":1}]},"G3813":{"id":"G3813","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G3813","disambiguated_id":"G3813 =","unique_id":"G3813","headword":"παιδίον","transliteration":"paidion","lexical_morphology":"G:N-N","gloss_en":"child","definition_en":"παιδίον, -ου, τό dimin, of παῖς, \n [in LXX chiefly for יֶלֶד, also for נַעַר, בֵּן, etc., frequently in To in ref. to full-grown youth ;] \na young child, a little one: Mat.2:8-9, 11, ff., Luk.1:59, 66 1:76, 80 2:17, 27 2:40, Jhn.16:21, Heb.11:23; of older children, Mat.18:2, 4-5, Mrk.5:39-41 7:30 9:24, 36, Luk.9:47-48 18:17, Jhn.4:49; in pl., Mat.11:16 14:21 15:38 18:3 19:13-14, Mrk.7:28 10:13 ff., Luk.7:32 11:7 18:16, Heb.2:13-14 Metaphorical, 1Co.14:20. Colloq. in familiar address (as Eng. colloq., \"lads \"-see M, Pr., 170n and Irish use of \"boys\"): Jhn.21:5, 1Jn.2:13 Jn 2:18 Jn 3:7 †\n SYN.: see: παῖς (AS)","source_line":3931}],"occurrence_count":52,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"menino","count":20},{"gloss":"crianças","count":10},{"gloss":"criança","count":9},{"gloss":"menina","count":4},{"gloss":"filhos","count":4},{"gloss":"filhinhos","count":3},{"gloss":"meninos","count":2}]},"G427":{"id":"G427","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G0427","disambiguated_id":"G0427 =","unique_id":"G0427","headword":"ἄνευ","transliteration":"aneu","lexical_morphology":"G:PREP","gloss_en":"without","definition_en":"ἄνευ \n prep. with genitive (rarer than χωρίς, which see; cf. Ellic. on Eph.2:12; MM, VGT, 42), \n without: Mat.10:29, 1Pe.3:1 4:9.†\n (AS)","source_line":533}],"occurrence_count":3,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"sem","count":2},{"gloss":"vontade","count":1}]},"G4334":{"id":"G4334","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G4334","disambiguated_id":"G4334 =","unique_id":"G4334","headword":"προσέρχομαι","transliteration":"proserchomai","lexical_morphology":"G:V","gloss_en":"to come near/agree","definition_en":"προσ-έρχομαι \n [in LXX for קָרַב, נָגַשׁ, etc. ;] \nto approach, draw near: absol., Mat.4:11, Luk.9:42, al.; with infin., Mat.24:1, al.; with dative loc., Heb.12:18, 22; dative of person(s), Mat.5:1, and freq., Jhn.12:21, al.; ptcp., προσελθών, with indic., Mat.8:2, and freq., Mrk.1:31, Luk.7:14, al.; π. αὐτῷ, with indic., Mat.4:3, Mrk.6:35, \n Metaphorical, \n __(a) of approaching God: absol. (Lev.21:17, Deu.21:5, al.), Heb.10:1, 22; τ. θεῷ, Heb.7:25 11:6; τ. θρόνῳ τ. χάριτος, Heb.4:16; πρὸς Χριστόν, 1Pe.2:4; \n __(b) in sense not found elsewhere (Field, Notes, 211), to consent to: ὑγιαίνουσι λόγοις, 1Ti.6:3 \n (AS)","source_line":4464}],"oc